From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:38:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Say "Killed: out of memory" for a child the kernel ended for
 lack of memory

On Redox the kernel ends a process with SIGKILL when memory runs out,
and procmgr lists it in /scheme/proc/oom. When a foreground child ends
with SIGKILL and its PID is in that list, ion now prints
"ion: Killed: out of memory (process <pid>)" instead of "process (<pid>)
ended by signal SIGKILL", so the person at the terminal learns why the
program vanished (redox-rpi#791). Other systems are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
